{
  "an6.46:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 6.46 ",
  "an6.46:0.2": "5. About Dhammika ",
  "an6.46:0.3": "By Mahācunda ",
  "an6.46:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "an6.46:1.2": "At one time Venerable Mahācunda was staying in the land of the Cetis at Sahajāti. ",
  "an6.46:1.3": "There he addressed the mendicants: ",
  "an6.46:1.4": "“Reverends, mendicants!” ",
  "an6.46:1.5": "“Reverend,” they replied. ",
  "an6.46:1.6": "Venerable Mahācunda said this: ",
  "an6.46:2.1": "“Take a case where mendicants who practice discernment of principles rebuke mendicants who practice absorption: ",
  "an6.46:2.2": "‘They say, “We practice absorption meditation! We practice absorption meditation!” And they meditate and concentrate and contemplate and ruminate. ",
  "an6.46:2.3": "Why do they practice absorption meditation? In what way do they practice absorption meditation? How do they practice absorption meditation?’ ",
  "an6.46:2.4": "In this case the mendicants who practice discernment of principles are not inspired, and the mendicants who practice absorption are not inspired. And they’re not acting for the welfare and happiness of the people, for the people, for the benefit, welfare, and happiness of gods and humans. ",
  "an6.46:3.1": "Now, take a case where mendicants who practice absorption meditation rebuke mendicants who practice discernment of principles: ",
  "an6.46:3.2": "‘They say, “We practice discernment of principles! We practice discernment of principles!” But they’re haughty, inso